Enhancement: Add timeouts for request headers and idle connections

rest-server did not limit how long a client may take to send a request, nor
how long an idle keep-alive connection is kept open. A client could hold
connections open indefinitely, each costing a goroutine and a file
descriptor, until the server ran out of file descriptors and legitimate
clients were no longer served. This did not require valid credentials.

rest-server now closes a connection if the request headers do not arrive
within 30 seconds or if a keep-alive connection is idle for more than two
minutes. If rest-server rejects a request without reading its body, for
example because of missing credentials, it now closes the connection instead
of waiting for the client to send the rest of the body. Uploads and downloads
are not affected by these timeouts.

https://github.com/restic/rest-server/issues/408
